# nr-office-formula-core: what the wiring applies (nothing here was compiled: cargo was not run)

New crate native/core/crates/mixdog-xlsx-formula (written complete: Cargo.toml, src/{lib,token,parse,eval,value,coerce,registry}.rs,
src/functions/mod.rs, tests/twin_engine.rs). Dependencies: mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base (dev: with feature test-support),
mixdog-workspace-hack, serde_json (dev). No third-party crate is added.

## 1. native/core/Cargo.toml (hot file)

In `[workspace] members`, after the line `    "crates/mixdog-office-base",`:

    "crates/mixdog-xlsx-formula",

In `[workspace.dependencies]`, after the line `mixdog-office-base = { path = "crates/mixdog-office-base" }`:

    mixdog-xlsx-formula = { path = "crates/mixdog-xlsx-formula" }

(The crate's own Cargo.toml does not use that entry; the consumers, nr-office-xlsx-* tasks, do: `mixdog-xlsx-formula = { workspace = true }`.)

## 2. Cargo.lock and mixdog-workspace-hack (hot files)

`cargo update --workspace --offline` adds the package `mixdog-xlsx-formula` (dependencies: mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base,
mixdog-workspace-hack, serde_json); `cargo hakari generate` then lists it if the hack needs it (the crate pulls no third-party
feature of its own).

